    term: "Embedding Dimension",
    symbol: "d_model = 1280",
    category: "Model Architecture",
    formal: "The width of the vector carried at every sequence position through the transformer. WhAM uses 1280 for both the coarse and c2f stacks. This width dominates parameter count — attention and feed-forward weights scale with its square — and it is also the dimensionality of the embeddings extracted for downstream classification.",
    eli5: "Every slice of sound gets described by a list of 1280 numbers — that is the model's entire vocabulary for saying what is happening at one instant. Wider means more nuance, but cost grows with the square: doubling the width roughly quadruples the weights. It is also the number you inherit when you pull embeddings out for classification, so every downstream probe in this project works on 1280-number fingerprints, against 768 for AVES. Not a fair-fight comparison on its own — wider representations have an advantage that has nothing to do with knowing about whales.",
