    term: "Layers / Depth",
    symbol: "20 coarse, 16 c2f",
    category: "Model Architecture",
    formal: "The number of stacked transformer blocks. The coarse model runs 20; the coarse-to-fine model runs 16, on the reasoning that adding spectral detail to a fixed skeleton is an easier problem than inventing the skeleton. Depth matters for probing, since intermediate layers often carry more transferable structure than the final one.",
    eli5: "Depth is how many times the sound gets rewritten on its way through. Early layers deal in local facts — \"this is a sharp transient\" — while later layers deal in whole-clip facts like \"this is a five-click rhythm with a pause after the second.\" Middle layers hold the most useful mix, which is why the embedding extractor taps layer 10 of 20 rather than the end. The detailing model gets away with 16 layers instead of 20 because adding texture to a fixed skeleton is a genuinely easier job than inventing the skeleton.",
    seeAlso: ["transformer", "hidden-activations", "coarse-to-fine"],
