    formal: "Feature-wise Linear Modulation — a mechanism for conditioning a network on external information by predicting per-channel scale and shift parameters. The plumbing is present throughout the VampNet stack but is inert in WhAM: `r_cond_dim` is 0 in every shipped checkpoint, and the constructor asserts it must be. Worth knowing about only so you do not mistake it for an active control surface.",
    eli5: "A dial the original architecture left on the box for steering generation from outside — \"make it more of this kind of sound.\" In WhAM the dial is wired to nothing: the code checks it is zero and refuses to run otherwise, so the conditioning layers sit in every block doing arithmetic that changes nothing. It is worth knowing this before you go looking for a way to condition generation on social unit or coda type. There is no such input. Everything you can steer, you steer through masking.",
