    category: "Model Architecture",
    formal: "A memory-efficient fused attention kernel that avoids materialising the full attention matrix. It is CUDA-only, and it ships disabled in every WhAM checkpoint. That single fact is why the model runs unmodified on Apple Silicon via MPS and on CPU — it was the one genuinely NVIDIA-bound component in the stack.",
    eli5: "A speed trick for attention that only works on NVIDIA graphics cards. WhAM ships with it switched off, which sounds like a downside but is precisely why the model runs on a Mac at all — it was the one component that genuinely required CUDA. Everything else was already device-agnostic. The trade is real: attention is slower and uses more memory without it. The catch worth remembering is that Apple's GPU and NVIDIA's do not produce bit-identical arithmetic, so a generation made here will not exactly match one made on the authors' machine even with the same seed.",
