    term: "Output Classifier",
    symbol: "1280 → 4096",
    category: "Model Architecture",
    formal: "The final projection turning each 1280-dimensional position vector into logits over the token vocabulary. For the coarse model that is 4 codebooks x 1024 entries = 4096 outputs per position; for c2f it is 10 predicted codebooks x 1024 = 10240. Implemented as a weight-normalised 1x1 convolution, which is just a linear layer applied identically at every time step.",
    eli5: "The last step, where the model finally commits. It takes its rich internal description of a moment and turns it into a scorecard: for each of the 1024 possible sound-stamps, how likely is this the right one? Everything before was thinking; this is answering. The coarse model fills in four such scorecards per slice, the detailing model ten. Note that it never outputs audio — it outputs catalogue numbers, and the codec turns those back into sound. That separation is why the model can be whale-specific while the thing making the actual noise was built for music.",
